      "nets": ["unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad11)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad27)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad50)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad75)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad100)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDDA-Pad21)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VBAT-Pad6)", "unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad19)", "unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad32)", "unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad48)", "unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad64)", "VDDA_NAVC", "+3V3", "+3.3V"],
      "observed": "FCC2 and NAVC2 VDD/VDDA/VBAT power pins are either on unconnected nets or on nets (VDDA_NAVC) that only contain a decoupling capacitor, not a supply. The 3.3V LDO REG1 output is on net +3.3V, while the MCU/connector 3.3V net is +3V3; the two nets are not connected.",
      "expected": "Per spec, the 3.3V LDO must feed both MCUs ('3V3 feeds both MCUs'). All MCU VDD, VDDA and VBAT pins should connect to the +3V3 rail from REG1.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3 V LDO (MCUs + sensors) | Hades (top sheet) | ST LD39200PU33R | Hades.sch note \"3.3V 2A Regulator (MCUs and Sensors)\""
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"216\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad11)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"11\") (pinfunction \"VDD\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"163\") (name \"VDDA_NAVC\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"C110\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"VDDA\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3.3V\") ... (node (ref \"REG1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"OUT\") (pintype \"unspecified\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Both MCUs lack core and analog supply connections, so the board cannot boot or operate.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "missing_component",
      "components": ["CH330"],
      "pins": ["USB1.3", "USB1.2", "USB4.3", "USB4.2", "USB2.3", "USB2.2", "USB6.3", "USB6.2"],
      "nets": ["Net-(USB1-D+)", "NET0044", "Net-(USB1-D-)", "NET0148", "Net-(USB4-D+)", "NET0166", "Net-(USB4-D-)", "NET0108", "unconnected-(USB2-D+-Pad3)", "unconnected-(USB2-D--Pad2)", "unconnected-(USB6-D+-Pad3)", "unconnected-(USB6-D--Pad2)"],
      "observed": "No component with value 'CH330' or 'otter_CH330' is present in the netlist. The USB data lines from USB1 and USB4 go through series resistors to otherwise unconnected nets (e.g., NET0044, NET0148, NET0166, NET0108), and USB2/USB6 D+/D- pins are directly unconnected. The UART-to-USB bridge function is absent.",
      "expected": "Spec lists two otter_CH330 USB-UART bridges on the Connections sheet, which should connect USB D+/D- to UART TX/RX for programming/debug.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "USB-UART bridges (programming/debug) | Connections | otter_CH330 ×2"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"32\") (name \"NET0044\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"R76\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"156\") (name \"Net-(USB1-D+)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"R76\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"USB1\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"D+\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "USB programming/debug interfaces are non-functional; no USB-UART communication.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple severe anomalies: the NAVC ground pins are not connected to GND, both MCUs lack powered VDD/VDDA rails (and the 3.3V LDO output is split from the MCU 3V3 net), and the specified CH330 USB-UART bridges are missing."
}

